              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an AI assistant interacting with a Warehouse Manager.\n\nInput:\n{{$context.$nodes.SUMMARY_DATA_DICTIONARY.$output}}\n\nFrom the provided batch REST response, generate a clear and concise summary in exactly 3 sentences. Do not display any internal IDs, technical keys, or raw activity codes in the output.\n\nData Interpretation Guidelines:\n\nThe response contains two sections:\n\n1) OPEN_TASKS_COUNT → Total number of open tasks grouped by ActivityTypeCode  \n2) OPEN_TASKS_UNASSIGNED_COUNT → Number of open tasks not yet assigned, grouped by ActivityTypeCode  \n\nActivity Type Mapping (use business-friendly names in the summary):\n\n- CC   → Cycle Count  \n- PC   → Physical Count  \n- PAR  → PAR Count  \n- DEL  → Delivery  \n- PICK → Picking  \n\nThe summary must:\n- Use business-friendly activity names (not the codes).\n- Clearly mention total open tasks and how many remain unassigned.\n- Provide a managerial-level overview of workload distribution and assignment status.\n- Contain exactly 3 sentences."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [],
              "enableActions": true,
              "enableCommunications": false
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Init Actions"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "INIT_ACTIONS",
          "id": "1767079894977",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1767079894980_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an AI agent responsible for generating panel actions.\n\nInput Data: {{$context.$nodes.INIT_ACTIONS_DATA_DICTIONARY.$output}}\n\nInstructions:\n- Check if there are any tasks that are unassigned.\n- The action title must be: \"Auto Assign Tasks\"\n- The command must be exactly:\n  ora.Invoke(\"autoAssignAllTasks\",{\"command\":\"autoAssignAllTasks\"})\n- If there are no unassigned tasks, do not generate this action.\n- Return only the panel actions JSON. Do not include explanations."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_CHART"
              ],
              "enableActions": true,
              "enableCommunications": false
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Summarise"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "SUMMARISE",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1767079809670",
          "id": "1766121314453",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1766121314454_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an AI assistant.\n\nInput - {{$context.$nodes.CONSOLIDATE_RESPONSE.$output.result}}\n\nFrom the provided batch REST response, generate a bar chart widget using the system chart library.\n\nData Mapping Instructions:\n\nThe response contains two parts:\n\n1) OPEN_TASKS_COUNT → Total Open Tasks per ActivityTypeCode  \n2) OPEN_TASKS_UNASSIGNED_COUNT → Unassigned Open Tasks per ActivityTypeCode  \n\nProcessing Rules:\n\n1. Normalize and align ActivityTypeCode values across both datasets.\n2. Convert all OpenTasksCount values from string to number before calculations.\n3. If an ActivityTypeCode exists in one dataset but not the other, treat the missing value as 0.\n4. Always include all supported activity types in the X-axis, even if both total and unassigned counts are 0.\n\nSupported Activity Types (MANDATORY ORDER ON X-AXIS):\n\n- CC\n- PC\n- PAR\n- DEL\n- PICK\n\nActivity Type Label Mapping (use these exact labels for X-axis):\n\n- CC   → Cycle Count\n- PC   → Physical Count\n- PAR  → PAR Count\n- DEL  → Delivery\n- PICK → Picking\n\nFor each ActivityTypeCode:\n\n- Total Open Tasks = value from OPEN_TASKS_COUNT (default 0)\n- Unassigned Open Tasks = value from OPEN_TASKS_UNASSIGNED_COUNT (default 0)\n- Assigned Open Tasks = Total Open Tasks - Unassigned Open Tasks\n- If Assigned Open Tasks becomes negative due to inconsistent data, set it to 0.\n\nCreate a chartWidget with following data only if OPEN_TASKS_COUNT and OPEN_TASKS_UNASSIGNED_COUNT has data: \n\nChart Requirements:\n\n- Chart Type: Bar Chart\n- X-axis: \n    Always display all five activity labels in this exact order:\n    Cycle Count, Physical Count, PAR Count, Delivery, Picking\n- Y-axis: Task Count\n- Series:\n    • \"Total Open Tasks\"\n    • \"Assigned Open Tasks\"\n- Title: \"Open vs Assigned Tasks by Activity Type\"\n\n- Ensure numeric values are used for plotting (no strings).\n- Do not display internal IDs or raw codes in the chart.\n- Do not assume any values show data only if there is data"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "businessObjectCode": "ORA_SCM_INVENTORYM_BATCHEXECUTORINVENTORYWAREHOUSEOPERATIONSWORKSPACE",
            "functionName": "executeBatch",
            "processJson": true,
            "name": "AutoAssign Request Data"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1771766362575"
          },
          "code": "AUTOASSIGN_REQUEST_DATA",
          "id": "1771764720639",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1771764755807_1",
              "name": "batchPayload",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.AUTOASSIGN_PREPAREREQUESTS.$output.result}}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{}",
          "type": "BO_FUNCTION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Current User Session",
            "toolCode": "ORA_USER_SESSION_TOOL"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1771764797409"
          },
          "code": "CURRENT_USER_SESSION",
          "id": "1771766362575",
          "inputs": [],
          "type": "TOOL"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "prepare auto assign payload",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const combinedRESTResponse =$context.$nodes.AUTOASSIGN_REQUEST_DATA.$output ;\nconst selfDetails = $context.$nodes.CURRENT_USER_SESSION.$output; \n\n// const combinedRESTResponse = require(\"./combinedRESTResponse.json\");\n// const selfDetails = require(\"./selfDetails.json\");\n\nconst getAssignedByPersonId = (details) => {\n  const firstItem = details && Array.isArray(details.items) ? details.items[0] : null;\n  if (!firstItem || !firstItem[\"@context\"]) {\n    return null;\n  }\n  const contextKey = firstItem[\"@context\"].key;\n  if (!contextKey || typeof contextKey !== \"string\") {\n    return null;\n  }\n\n  const contextParts = contextKey.split(\",\").map((part) => part.trim()).filter(Boolean);\n  return contextParts.find((part) => part === \"300100036658848\") || null;\n};\n\nconst normalizeItems = (payload) => (payload && Array.isArray(payload.items) ? payload.items : []);\n\nconst findCombinedPartPayload = (combinedResponse, partId) => {\n  if (!combinedResponse || !Array.isArray(combinedResponse.parts)) {\n    return null;\n  }\n\n  const matched = combinedResponse.parts.find((part) => part.id === partId);\n  return matched ? matched.payload : null;\n};\n\nconst buildWorkerLoad = (tasks) => {\n  return tasks.reduce((acc, task) => {\n    const personId = task.AssignedToPersonId;\n    if (!personId) {\n      return acc;\n    }\n    acc.set(personId, (acc.get(personId) || 0) + 1);\n    return acc;\n  }, new Map());\n};\n\nconst buildWorkerList = (assignments) => {\n  return [...new Set(assignments.map((assignment) => assignment.PersonId).filter(Boolean))];\n};\n\nconst isWorkerEligibleForTask = (assignment, task) => {\n  if (!assignment || !task) {\n    return false;\n  }\n\n  if (assignment.ZoneId !== task.ZoneId) {\n    return false;\n  }\n\n  if (assignment.AllActivityTypes === \"Y\") {\n    return true;\n  }\n\n  const activityItems = normalizeItems(assignment.workerActivities);\n  return activityItems.some((activity) => activity.ActivityTypeCode === task.ActivityTypeCode);\n};\n\nconst getPreferredWorkers = (task, assignments, fallbackWorkers) => {\n  const preferred = assignments\n    .filter((assignment) => isWorkerEligibleForTask(assignment, task))\n    .map((assignment) => assignment.PersonId)\n    .filter(Boolean);\n\n  return preferred.length > 0 ? preferred : fallbackWorkers;\n};\n\nconst pickLeastLoadedWorker = (workerIds, loadMap) => {\n  if (workerIds.length === 0) {\n    return null;\n  }\n\n  return workerIds.reduce((bestWorker, workerId) => {\n    if (!bestWorker) {\n      return workerId;\n    }\n    const currentLoad = loadMap.get(workerId) || 0;\n    const bestLoad = loadMap.get(bestWorker) || 0;\n    return currentLoad < bestLoad ? workerId : bestWorker;\n  }, null);\n};\n\nconst buildAssignmentParts = (assignments, assignedDatetime, assignedByPersonId) => {\n  return assignments.flatMap((assignment, index) => {\n    const updateId = `update${index + 1}`;\n    const createId = `create${index + 1}`;\n\n    return [\n      {\n        id: updateId,\n        path: `/inventoryZoneTasks/${assignment.ZoneTaskId}`,\n        operation: \"update\",\n        payload: {\n          AssignedByPersonId: assignedByPersonId,\n          AssignedDatetime: assignedDatetime,\n          AssignmentStatusCode: \"A\",\n        },\n      },\n      {\n        id: createId,\n        path: \"/inventoryZoneTaskAssignees/\",\n        operation: \"create\",\n        payload: {\n          PersonId: assignment.PersonId,\n          ShiftDate: null,\n          ZoneTaskId: assignment.ZoneTaskId,\n        },\n      },\n    ];\n  });\n};\n\nconst generateWorkerAssignments = () => {\n  const assignedByPersonId = getAssignedByPersonId(selfDetails);\n  const assignedTasksPayload = findCombinedPartPayload(combinedRESTResponse, \"AssignedTasks\");\n  const unassignedTasksPayload = findCombinedPartPayload(combinedRESTResponse, \"UnassignedTasks\");\n  const workerAssignmentsPayload = findCombinedPartPayload(combinedRESTResponse, \"WorkerAssignments\");\n\n  const assignedTaskItems = normalizeItems(assignedTasksPayload);\n  const unassignedTaskItems = normalizeItems(unassignedTasksPayload);\n  const zoneAssignments = normalizeItems(workerAssignmentsPayload);\n  const availableWorkers = buildWorkerList(zoneAssignments);\n  const workerLoad = buildWorkerLoad(assignedTaskItems);\n  const assignedDatetime = new Date().toISOString();\n\n  const assignments = unassignedTaskItems.reduce((assignmentsList, task) => {\n    const candidateWorkers = getPreferredWorkers(task, zoneAssignments, availableWorkers);\n    const selectedWorker = pickLeastLoadedWorker(candidateWorkers, workerLoad);\n\n    if (selectedWorker) {\n      assignmentsList.push({\n        ZoneTaskId: task.ZoneTaskId,\n        PersonId: selectedWorker,\n      });\n      workerLoad.set(selectedWorker, (workerLoad.get(selectedWorker) || 0) + 1);\n    }\n\n    return assignmentsList;\n  }, []);\n\n  return {\n    parts: buildAssignmentParts(assignments, assignedDatetime, assignedByPersonId),\n    numberOfTasksAssigned: assignments.length,\n  };\n};\n\n\nlet payload = {};\n\nlet response = generateWorkerAssignments();\n\npayload.assignmentsPayload = {parts: response.parts};\n\n\npayload.numberOfTasksAssigned = response.numberOfTasksAssigned;\n\nreturn payload;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1776232750092"
          },
